  "forbiddenFieldNamePatterns": [
    "(?i)(^|_)auth(orization)?($|_)",
    "(?i)(^|_)cookie($|_)",
    "(?i)(^|_)(token|bearer)($|_)",
    "(?i)(^|_)secret($|_)",
    "(?i)(^|_)private[_-]?key($|_)",
    "(?i)(^|_)password($|_)",
    "(?i)(^|_)(req|request|res|response)_body($|_)",
    "(?i)(^|_)(email|user_email)($|_)"
  ],
  "forbiddenValuePatterns": [
    "(?i)(authorization|cookie|set-cookie|bearer\\s+[a-z0-9._~+/=-]{16,}|api[_-]?key\\s*[=:\"]|secret\\s*[=:\"]|password\\s*[=:\"]|private key)"
  ],
  "urlFieldsMustNotContainQueryOrFragment": ["view_url", "resource_url"],
  "notes": [
    "requiredNativeFields is intentionally short: only fields observed present on every RUM record type (view/action/error/resource) in this repo's own Stage 8 regression. Everything else is conditionalNativeFieldGroups, keyed by the record's own 'type' field, because OpenObserve's stream schema is additive-only and cannot itself prove a field is still produced by the current SDK (docs/openobserve-v0.91-stream-capabilities.md capability #5) — only a fresh canary can.",
    "This contract intentionally does NOT freeze the native schema as a strict allow-list: new optional native fields from a future @openobserve/browser-rum version are expected and are SAFE_ADDITIVE_NATIVE_DRIFT, not a failure, as long as they are not in forbiddenFieldNames/forbiddenFieldNamePatterns and do not change an existing required field's type.",
    "'_rumreplay' (or any other session-replay stream) is not a canonical stream and must never receive data — see docs/session-replay-security-decision.md (Stage 11, still Security Blocked)."
  ]
}
